<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <MSBuildAllProjects>$(MSBuildAllProjects);$(MSBuildThisFileFullPath)</MSBuildAllProjects>
    <HasSharedItems>true</HasSharedItems>
    <SharedGUID>{A5B6C7D8-E9F0-4A1B-2C3D-4E5F6A7B8C9D}</SharedGUID>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Label="Configuration">
    <Import_RootNamespace>Birko.Data.Migrations.InfluxDB</Import_RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- External dependency: InfluxDB.Client — CONSUMER-SUPPLIED for this project alone:

         <PackageReference Include="InfluxDB.Client" Version="5.*" />

       Every other Birko project that wraps a library declares it, so importing the project is all a
       consumer has to do. This is the second documented exception (the first is Birko.Health.Redis),
       and it is here for the same reason: this project uses the driver directly and needs nothing
       from Birko.Data.InfluxDB — no type of its is referenced, and its own test project does not
       import it.

       It cannot declare, because Birko.Data.InfluxDB.projitems does and Birko.Sandbox imports both:
       two PackageReference items in one project file is NU1504, an error under the sweep's
       -warnaserror. And it must not take a dependency on Birko.Data.InfluxDB purely to inherit the
       declaration, because a consumer takes only the subset it needs.

       Declare the line above only if you import this project without Birko.Data.InfluxDB (TASK-234). -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)InfluxMigrationStore.cs" />
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)InfluxMigrationRunner.cs" />
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Context\InfluxDBMigrationContext.cs" />
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Context\InfluxDBSchemaBuilder.cs" />
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Context\InfluxDBDataMigrator.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
